sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): stage 2 of the command development pipeline. A task VM, where an agent or Nick develops a command and the proof cases run too, is a copy of the host's base VM snapshot with a fresh identity, named `<node>-tvm-<n>` by its slot under the host's `max_vms`. The base holds everything installed and ready: orbit-agent, the Pi server, the tools, Swamp, sshd and UFW, a warm checkout of main with `vendor/` and `node_modules/`, and the nested fleet (a Gateway with Swamp, an app-dev Node, an app-prod Node) as Incus system containers that start with the VM, with a `base` snapshot each for the proof. The containers mount the outer VM's checkout as a disk device, so an edit reaches them at once. The task start: docs/cli/tasks/provision.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 2 · development environment
  %% kind: pipeline.2-development-environment
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=hub tone=gray
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=task VM tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=gray
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>provision run
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>outer · operator
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>3 containers
  Note over GW: Take a slot<br/>mint its identity
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - an external task group in `todo`, a free slot under a host's `max_vms` and a promoted base snapshot on that host
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group holds the slot; its Node, WireGuard key, host key, agent secret, Pi token and model key are new, and the public keys are pinned on the Node
  %%> - a proof is placed only on a host whose promoted image holds every change of what the image carries, up to the merge base of the proof commit with main (`TaskVmImageInputs`); otherwise the admission answers `tasks.capacity_unavailable` and names the release the host's image comes from
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>tasks provision
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the same run for a person, an agent or a CI proof
  SW->>H: Create and start the VM<br/>copy of the base snapshot
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus copy` of the host's base snapshot and a clone of its seed snapshot (ZFS clones), an identity volume with the identity and keys, `incus start`; the base's orbit-identity unit applies it at boot; the containers start with the VM
  SW->>HUB: Add the hub peer<br/>peer file · wg addconf
  %%> Runs beside the step before it: Swamp starts both at once.
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds the new WireGuard key as a peer of the hub while the VM boots
  SW->>VM: Converge and branch<br/>the release's converge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the converge of the release refresh: a no-op on a current image; it catches up a small delta when main moved since the last release
  %%> - then the new task branch on the warm checkout, at the group's start commit
  %%> - the outer VM is the operator of the nested fleet; that operator key belongs to the nested network only and is baked with the fleet, so it is no part of the VM's identity
  SW->>VM: Reach the VM by WireGuard<br/>ssh from 209 · pinned key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the path every later step takes: ssh from a Swamp worker to the VM's WireGuard address
  SW->>VM: Check ready<br/>one exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one exec checks the agent, Pi, the tunnel and the three containers; Swamp's `assert` decides
  SW-->>GW: Environment ready<br/>terminal event
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group runs on the slot; the proof (stage 3) or the proof CI (stage 4) uses the fleet
  %%> - target under 30 s from admission
  loop while the author develops
    VM->>NT: Edit, test, call the CLI<br/>the checkout is shared
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the author edits and runs tests on the outer VM; PHP in the nested containers sees the change on the next request
    %%> - the candidate CLI on the outer VM talks to the nested Gateway as the operator
    %%> - after a new migration, the author runs the migrations in the nested Gateway
  end
  opt the author wants a clean fleet
    SW->>NT: Restore the base snapshot<br/>a reboot · 5–16 s
    %%> What it keeps:
    %%> - the outer VM, Pi and the checkout
  end
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>and its seed clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - at the end of the group the VM, its seed clone and its identity volume go, the hub peer is removed, the claim's model key is revoked and the Gateway deletes the Node (docs/cli/tasks/cancel.mmd)
